 "notes": "SWP Beit Jubr et Tahtani (Mem III p. 24; printed pp. 190-191) is the site of Nigro N36 'Beit Jabr et-Tahtani' (890 m; same name, and N36 cites Conder-Kitchener 1883, 190-191); its birkeh 'immediately south of the fort' coded at grid N36 (judgment call). SWP Tell es Sultan entry (Mem III p. 220) describes Tell es Sultan, not in the 2 km WBADB/Nigro lists; ignored, incl. Warren's graves; its Tellul Abu el 'Aleik paragraph has no pool, pit or grave. Own-row 'basin and bath' of the Rom bathhouses coded pool_def unclear. 'Ritual baths' and 'baths' coded pool_def unclear. Nigro N7 'pits (post-Herodian Period: 2nd century AD)' coded U (2nd century straddles 135 CE). N31 is the unit itself (12 m, bearing invalid). Rock shelters and niches not coded. Herodian 'columbarium' tower is built, not coded."
